# Monsters, with room to walk (§7.1's scripted agents).
#
# A fixture, deliberately separate from doors.map. Both maps want monsters in
# them and they want OPPOSITE things from them: doors.map needs them present but
# inert, because a monster that chases eventually arrives wherever the door test
# is standing and shoulders it off the door it is opening; this map needs them
# awake, because what it tests is that they chase, that they shoot, and that the
# shots are stopped by walls.
#
# Two rooms and a doorway between them, so line of sight is a real question:
#
#   room A (the player)  --[opening]--  room B (the monsters)
#
# The opening is a gap in a shared wall rather than a door sector. Nothing here
# opens, so there is nothing for a script to move, and a shot that reaches the
# player has genuinely travelled through the gap rather than through the wall.

sector floor 0 ceil 4 tag 1 light 200 floortex FLOOR4_8 ceiltex CEIL3_5
  vertex 0 0    wall tex STARTAN3
  vertex 20 0   wall tex STARTAN3
  vertex 20 8   neighbor 1
  vertex 20 12  wall tex STARTAN3
  vertex 20 20  wall tex STARTAN3
  vertex 0 20   wall tex STARTAN3
end

sector floor 0 ceil 4 tag 2 light 180 floortex FLOOR4_8 ceiltex CEIL3_5
  vertex 20 0   wall tex STARTAN3
  vertex 40 0   wall tex STARTAN3
  vertex 40 20  wall tex STARTAN3
  vertex 20 20  wall tex STARTAN3
  vertex 20 12  neighbor 0
  vertex 20 8   wall tex STARTAN3
end

# Doom's player at 1/48, matching every other converted map here.
body radius 0.3333 height 1.1667

script scripts/mob_vocab.lua
script scripts/mobs.lua
script mobs/doom_monsters.lua
script monsters_lines.lua

spawn start 5 10 1
